/*
2. HEADER VS Code SNIPPET SCRIPT 

You can create a custom snippet that automatically fills in your name and inserts the exact date dynamically [1].
1. Go to File > Preferences > Configure User Snippets (or Ctrl+Shift+P / Cmd+Shift+P and type User Snippets).
2. Select c (for C files).
3. Paste the following snippet configuration inside the JSON braces:



{

	"C File Header": {
    "prefix": "doc-header",
    "body": [
        "/*******************************************************************************",
        " * @file        ${TM_FILENAME}",
        " * @author      VS",
        " * @date        ${CURRENT_YEAR}-${CURRENT_MONTH}-${CURRENT_DATE}",
        " * @brief       ${1:Description of the file}",
        " *******************************************************************************/",
        "$0"
    ],
    "description": "Inserts a standard file header comment with name and current date"
}

• How to use it: Open a .c file, type doc-header, and hit Tab or Enter. VS Code will automatically generate the block, pull the exact current filename, and stamp today's date (2026-10-14).
*/

